AIM:
Given two strings s and goal, return true if s can become goal after some number of left-shifts (moving the first character to the end).
If possible → return true.
Otherwise → return false.
JAVA CODE:
public class RotateString {
    public static boolean rotateString(String s, String goal) {
        // Lengths must match
        if (s.length() != goal.length()) return false;
        // Check if goal is a substring of s+s
        return (s + s).contains(goal);
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String s1 = "abcde";
        String goal1 = "cdeab";
        System.out.println(rotateString(s1, goal1)); // Output: true

        String s2 = "abcde";
        String goal2 = "abced";
        System.out.println(rotateString(s2, goal2)); // Output: false
    }
}
INPUT:
s = "abcde"
goal = "cdeab"
OUTPUT:
true
